Plazo Protocol
==============

Licensing in this repository is per directory. There is no single licence
covering the whole tree, and the boundary is enforced in CI by
`tools/check-boundaries.mjs` — the open tree may not import from the closed
tree, so the open half can be split out with `git subtree split` and still
build.

Apache License 2.0 — see `LICENSE-APACHE`
----------------------------------------

  contracts/            The protocol itself.
  packages/plan-core/   Plan identity, nonce, schedule and strip derivation.
  packages/events/      The frozen event schema.
  packages/arc-verify/  The Arc primitive verification gate.
  packages/keeper/      The reference keeper.

These are open for a reason that is load-bearing rather than promotional. A
borrower holding a signed authorization strip must be able to recompute the
plan id, the payee address and every nonce from the disclosed terms alone,
without Plazo's cooperation. If verifying the deal required running Plazo's
server, "the signed bytes commit to the disclosed deal" would be a claim
rather than a property.

The keeper is open for the same kind of reason. The protocol's central claim
is that collections do not depend on the operator — and a keeper that only
Plazo can run is an operator dependency wearing a different name. It reads
the chain and nothing else: no Plazo API, no index, no allowlist.

Proprietary — see `LICENSE-PROPRIETARY`
---------------------------------------

  apps/                 Product surfaces.
  services/             Operator services.
  packages/ui/          The design system.

All rights reserved.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

Solidity dependencies are vendored at pinned commits by
`tools/install-libs.sh` and carry their own licences: forge-std (MIT),
OpenZeppelin Contracts (MIT), Solady (MIT).
